Subject: [PATCH] DV GL: treat Mesa's sRGB-capable scanout as linear

Mesa gives desktop default framebuffers sRGB formats, so the encoding
query returns GL_SRGB although writes stay linear until
GL_FRAMEBUFFER_SRGB is enabled. Without this the scanout is refused
and every Dolby Vision frame failed at the base-layer import.

--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoRenderers/DVBridgeGLES.cpp
@@ -1623,6 +1623,10 @@ bool CDVBridgeGLES::RebindOutputSurface(bool hdr10, bool sdr, unsigned int frame
       GL_FRAMEBUFFER_ATTACHMENT_BLUE_SIZE, &blue);
   glGetFramebufferAttachmentParameteriv(GL_FRAMEBUFFER, attachment,
       GL_FRAMEBUFFER_ATTACHMENT_COLOR_ENCODING, &encoding);
+  // Mesa gives desktop default framebuffers sRGB formats; writes stay linear until
+  // GL_FRAMEBUFFER_SRGB is enabled.
+  if (encoding == GL_SRGB && !glIsEnabled(GL_FRAMEBUFFER_SRGB))
+    encoding = GL_LINEAR;
 #else
   glGetIntegerv(GL_RED_BITS, &red);
   glGetIntegerv(GL_GREEN_BITS, &green);
